Read AGENTS.md, docs/SPEC.md (§3 key screens, §5, §7), docs/PLAN.md, docs/DECISIONS.md, the web app (web/src), the
report templates, backend replay/runner.py and the .mmrec format, and the simulator/scenario fixtures
(backend/tests/fixtures/sim_scenarios.py, Elm327Sim). The public judge site is live on Modal in replay-only mode. Two
problems seen on it today:
(a) The judge demo bundle (sim-healthy.mmrec) has ONE event, so judges see priors and a next-test list, not an
    investigation.
(b) The web UI is unstyled browser-default HTML. Demo quality is a large part of judging.

Write .agents/plans/M6B.md (under 140 lines):
1. A deterministic demo-bundle generator (scripts/make_demo_bundle.py) that drives the real backend end to end on the
   simulator's vacuum_leak scenario (and a second bundle for coil_unplugged): session start with tools + level,
   adapter fingerprint, DTC/PID evidence, planner-recommended tests performed in order with safety acks, posteriors
   converging (true hypothesis #1, p >= 0.8, <= 4 tests), one keyframe with Spark components + SAM overlay + second
   opinion, one manual-PDF SpecRange that decides an outcome, one engine-sound evidence (synthetic WAV), the report
   with a Wonder review. Every model output comes from the response cache recorded from REAL live calls (the existing
   live fixtures, plus a one-time owner-run script `scripts/record_demo_cache.py` that makes the few extra live calls
   needed and stores them), so replay is $0 and byte-identical. Label the bundles "simulated vehicle, real AI outputs".
   The real Ford bundles replace them by file drop later.
2. Web UI design pass: a coherent visual system (CSS variables, light + dark, a mechanic-friendly layout: top status
   bar with vehicle, adapter, level and budget; left timeline scrubber of events; center hypothesis chart with
   probability bands and the explanation trace on hover/click; right next-test card with safety checklist; evidence
   drawer with photo + SAM overlay and AI/DSP/manual badges), responsive down to phone width, no new heavy deps
   (plain CSS or one small, justified lib). The judge landing explains in two sentences what they're seeing and has
   one "Play the investigation" button that auto-plays the replay at 2x. The report page prints cleanly.
3. A first-run "60-second judge path" written into docs/JUDGES.md and mirrored on the landing.
Tests per item (offline), screenshots via headless Chrome (google-chrome is installed on the host, not in your
